No?

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:06.940
the drop yes all right corridor one five nine

00:02:10.870 --> 00:02:22.450
Lister shut up am I or me? well don't Lister don't hum and don't make any stupid

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:29.960
sounds with your cheeks Lister one more sound anything and you're

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:40.980
report the letter. What job number is this? Right, that's it. Lister, the third technician,

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:47.750
offense, obstructing a superior technician by humming, clicking and being quiet.

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:55.220
When the captain sees this, you're dead. Remember, I'm bored. Bored? This is essential routine

00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:59.970
maintenance. It's absolutely vital for the well-being of this crew, this mission and this...

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:17.420
ship. Dispenser 172 chicken soup nozzle clogged. Pass me a 14B, Lister. Lister, is this a 14B?

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:29.040
Does it look even remotely like a 14B? It's a 14B. This is a 14F. Are you blind?

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:57.540
It's my care lister. It's my career lister. I'm the one who gets it in the neck if an officer comes along, orders chicken soup and gets blackcurrant cordial with blancmange and two creams and a sugar. Chicken soup. Yep, that's working.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.660
anyway all this maintenance business the only reason they don't give this job to the service

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:10.780
robots is they've got a better union than us listen that is absolute nonsense right what's next

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:18.410
botanical gardens faulty porous circuit and corridor 147 sticking door true you know about

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:23.360
remember you rank below all four of those service robots even the one that's gone absolutely mad

00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:27.580
well this is a lot for long matey up up up that's where i'm going not until your passion

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:29.970
engineer's exam and you won't do that because you just go

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:35.410
there and flunk again. Lister, last time I only failed by the narrowest of narrow margins.

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:42.340
You what? You walked in there and wrote, I am a fish 400 times with a funny little dance and fainting.

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:48.290
That's a total lie. No, it's not. Peterson told me. No, it's not. Peterson told me. Lister,

00:04:48.410 --> 00:04:51.810
if you must know, what I did was I wrote a discourse on porous circuits, which was simply

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:57.420
too radical, too unconventional, too mold breaking for the examiners to accept. Yeah,

00:04:57.420 --> 00:04:58.440
Yeah, he said you were the fish.

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:01.840
Is that a cigarette you're smoking, Lister?

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:02.980
No, it's a chicken.

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:04.680
Right, you're on report.

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:07.810
Two times in as many minutes, Lister. I don't know.

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:09.140
Rimmer, Lister?

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:09.920
Yes, sir.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:11.700
Yo, Todd, want to get down!

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:13.480
Indeed.

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:16.220
Now, Rimmer, I'm just going through McIntyre's artefacts,

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:21.100
and I see that you've filed 247 complaints against Lister.

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:22.700
Yes, sir.

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:26.680
That's 123 counts of insulting a superior technician,

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:29.980
39 counts of dereliction of duty, 85...

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:33.810
Four counts of general insubordination and one count of mutiny.

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:34.410
Yes, sir.

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:35.960
Mutiny, Lister?

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:37.120
I stood on his toe.

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:39.080
Maliciously and with intent to wound.

00:05:39.260 --> 00:05:40.300
It was an accident.

00:05:40.780 --> 00:05:41.680
Lister, I put it to you.

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:44.280
How is it possible to stand on one small toe by accident?

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:45.520
You didn't stand on my toe at all.

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:47.060
You stood on my entire foot,

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:49.840
thereby obstructing a superior technician in pursuit of vital duty.

00:05:50.140 --> 00:05:52.580
But the vital duty was him to snap my guitar in half.

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:55.820
Whereupon you leapt from the top bunk onto the hole of my right foot.

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:56.280
All right, that's enough.

00:05:56.280 --> 00:05:57.900
Had it been a crisis situation, Lister,

00:05:58.040 --> 00:05:59.560
I would have had to perform my duties hopping.

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:02.210
Clearly putting the ship at risk, clearly therefore mutiny.

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:03.030
Finished.

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:06.500
However, I'm not a vindictive man, so I don't intend to apply for the death penalty.

00:06:06.870 --> 00:06:09.010
There are 169 people on board this ship.

00:06:09.110 --> 00:06:10.630
You, Rimmer, are over one man.

00:06:11.080 --> 00:06:12.100
Why can't you two get on?

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:13.440
You see, I try, sir.

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:15.510
I'm not an insubordinate man by nature.

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:19.830
I try and expect Rimmer and everything, but it's not easy, because he's such a smeghead.

00:06:21.410 --> 00:06:22.410
Did you hear that, sir?

00:06:22.970 --> 00:06:27.450
Lister, do you have any conception of the penalty for describing a superior technician as a smeghead?

00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:29.430
Oh, Rimmer.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.820
You are a snakehead.

00:06:34.310 --> 00:06:35.650
Respect so your career's over.

00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:37.310
Talk until you finish, you big-leg.

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:45.330
We're all gathered here today to pay our last respects to George McIntyre.

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:49.790
George was an excellent officer and as good a friend as anyone could ever hope to have.

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:53.200
And he'll be missed more deeply and more completely than he could ever know.

00:06:54.520 --> 00:06:57.080
And now commend his ashes to the stars he loves so much.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:00.440
Bye, George.

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:01.580
We'll miss you.

00:07:05.060 --> 00:07:10.040
This is a piece of music he specially requested.

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:11.260
Start the tape, please, Holly.

00:07:11.710 --> 00:07:13.190
I'll see you later on, yeah.

00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:18.960
That was McIntyre.

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:22.680
Bye, George.

00:07:22.990 --> 00:07:23.750
That was George?

00:07:25.300 --> 00:07:25.560
Really?

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:27.240
I thought it was Mary, Queen of Scots.

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:28.140
Oh, everybody first.

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:29.900
Hey, I was watching.

00:07:30.060 --> 00:07:36.390
Well, tough. You touch that guitar, Lister, I'll remove the E string and garrotte you with it.

00:07:36.990 --> 00:07:39.570
Can I do anything? Is it okay for breathe? Can I breathe?

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:45.860
Lister, I have an exam tomorrow which I intend to pass.

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:46.960
I know, yeah, by cheating.

00:07:47.380 --> 00:07:53.180
This is not cheating. It's merely an aid to memory. Helps me marshal the facts already in my command.

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:59.400
It does copy the entire textbooks onto your body. Why don't you hand your body in and let them mark that?

00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:03.750
Lister, do you think it's easy for someone like me to become an officer?

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:05.940
Someone who wasn't academy educated?

00:08:06.180 --> 00:08:08.120
Someone who didn't have the right knobby background?

00:08:08.610 --> 00:08:10.070
Someone who didn't have the right parents?

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:11.540
You didn't have the right parents?

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:13.130
Whose parents did you have?

00:08:14.950 --> 00:08:16.750
My parents. The wrong parents.

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:20.090
I'm just saying, you know, if you can't pass fair and square, why bother?

00:08:20.780 --> 00:08:23.260
Well, you would, Lister, because you've got no ambition, no drive.

00:08:23.260 --> 00:08:25.820
You're perfectly content to be the lowest rank on this ship.

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:27.700
I'm not the lowest rank on this ship.

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:29.560
What about the laboratory mice?

00:08:30.670 --> 00:08:32.670
Tell those mice to do something, they've got to jump to it.

00:08:32.910 --> 00:08:34.270
Yes, Mr. Lister, sir!

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:38.050
Lister, you are a nothing.

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:40.280
Not a nothing. I've got me plan.

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:43.830
What's that, the plan to be the slobbiest entity in the entire universe?

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:46.660
No, me five-year plan.

00:08:47.110 --> 00:08:50.310
You see, I'm going to do two more trips, and I've been saving up all me pay.

00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:51.310
Since when?

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:52.290
Since always.

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:56.230
That's why I never buy any soap or deodorant or socks or anything like that, you know?

00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:58.820
Anyway, I'm going to both have a little farm on Fiji.

00:08:59.260 --> 00:08:59.960
I'm going to get a...

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:01.780
With a sheep and a cow and breed horses.

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:06.840
With a sheep and a cow?

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:08.540
No, with horses and horses.

00:09:09.170 --> 00:09:09.770
On Fiji?

00:09:09.970 --> 00:09:11.530
Yeah, the prices there are unbelievable.

00:09:11.970 --> 00:09:16.150
Yes, because they had a volcanic eruption and now most of Fiji is three feet below sea level.

00:09:16.490 --> 00:09:17.970
It's only three feet they can wade.

00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:22.100
That's why the animals are going to have to be quite tall.

00:09:23.270 --> 00:09:26.910
Nice plan, Lister. Excellent plan. Brilliant plan, Lister.

00:09:27.550 --> 00:09:29.970
What about the sheep? What are you going to do? Buy them water?

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:35.780
water wings? Fit them with stilts? Better still, you could cross-breed them with dolphins

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:36.900
and have leaping mutton.

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:45.910
I get a drainage grant these days. Why bother, Lister? You could be the first man to produce

00:09:45.910 --> 00:09:51.050
wet-look knitwear. Look, this is why I never, ever said anything to you, because I knew

00:09:51.050 --> 00:09:56.220
you'd say something like this. Lister, you've got the brain of a cheese sandwich. Morning,

00:09:56.420 --> 00:09:59.780
farmer, Lister. I'm just popping down to the shops in my submarine.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:00.940
Can I buy you anything?

00:10:02.630 --> 00:10:06.570
The welcome-back George McIntyre reception is about to begin in the refectory.

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:08.830
George says he'd like to invite everybody,

00:10:09.130 --> 00:10:11.570
especially those who weren't able to attend his funeral.

00:10:31.950 --> 00:10:33.050
Have you seen the MSR?

00:10:33.250 --> 00:10:35.190
No, I'm waiting for it to come out in paperback.

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:39.360
Peterson, have you got a coin?

00:10:42.440 --> 00:10:44.460
I've just been shown this great new intelligence test.

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:45.280
What have you got to do?

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:47.440
Force the coin onto your forehead,

00:10:47.720 --> 00:10:50.080
and then the more times you can bang yourself on the head

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:52.540
without it falling off, the more intelligent you are.

00:10:52.740 --> 00:10:53.440
Are you going to go for it?

00:10:53.970 --> 00:10:55.190
He's going for it!

00:10:55.830 --> 00:10:57.970
Are you ready to feel it?

00:10:58.200 --> 00:10:58.400
Yep.

00:10:58.600 --> 00:10:59.140
Can you feel it?

00:10:59.240 --> 00:10:59.380
Yep.

00:10:59.580 --> 00:10:59.720
Can you feel it?

00:10:59.720 --> 00:10:59.980
Can you feel it?

00:11:05.420 --> 00:11:15.420
Folks, today is a day for both sadness and joy.

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:21.680
Sadness for the passing away of George and joy, because George is back with us, albeit

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:22.520
as a hologram.

00:11:23.260 --> 00:11:26.660
Now, some of you may not have traveled with a hologram before, so I ask you to treat him

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:29.960
as a normal man, because he is, in every respect, like...

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:35.860
George. He has George's personality and George's knowledge and experience. Of course, he can't lift

00:11:35.860 --> 00:11:41.680
anything or touch anything, so I ask you to cooperate with his request. And please, take every

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:55.260
care not to walk through him, not even when you're in a hurry. Thank you. I want to thank everybody

00:11:55.260 --> 00:11:59.900
for giving me such a marvelous funeral. I've just seen the vid.

00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:04.150
And I want to thank the captain for his beautiful eulogy.

00:12:04.470 --> 00:12:04.890
Beautiful.

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:08.340
But I still don't understand why he didn't use the one I wrote.

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:15.150
This must seem pretty spooky for everyone.

00:12:15.850 --> 00:12:19.760
But I don't want you to think of me as someone who's dead.

00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:23.560
More as someone who's no longer a threat to your marriages.

00:12:25.540 --> 00:12:27.460
I think Joe knows what I'm talking about.

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:35.750
As you know, Holly is only capable of sustaining one hologram.

00:12:36.450 --> 00:12:40.080
So my advice to anyone more vital to the mission than me is,

00:12:40.380 --> 00:12:41.900
if you die, I'll kill you.

00:12:49.360 --> 00:12:58.580
Flight coordinator George McIntyre.

00:13:09.310 --> 00:13:14.510
Just one thing before the disco, Holly tells me that he's sensed a non-human life form aboard.

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:15.730
Say it, it's Rimeh.

00:13:16.330 --> 00:13:20.150
We don't know what it is, Lister, so just be careful, okay?

00:13:20.710 --> 00:13:21.790
Say it, you're in Rimeh.

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:23.660
Ooh.

00:13:26.060 --> 00:13:29.680
Right, they're bound to ask the right thigh, which is 10%.

00:13:30.730 --> 00:13:33.730
They must ask the left thigh, which is 20%.

00:13:33.730 --> 00:13:37.180
They've got to ask one of the forearms,

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:38.600
which means I've passed already.

00:13:38.700 --> 00:13:39.860
Anything on the left chin's a bonus.

00:13:42.470 --> 00:13:42.910
Right.

00:13:43.690 --> 00:13:45.970
Cutie, current under tension is...

00:13:47.240 --> 00:13:48.560
Current under tension is equal.

00:13:49.580 --> 00:13:51.460
Current under tension is expandable.

00:13:52.460 --> 00:13:53.880
Current under tension is expensive.

00:13:55.050 --> 00:13:55.930
What does this mean?

00:13:56.880 --> 00:13:58.340
What does any of this mean?

00:13:58.400 --> 00:13:59.960
I've covered my body in...

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:04.380
complete and utter and total, absolute, nonsense gibberish!

00:14:06.180 --> 00:14:06.420
Urgh!

00:14:07.020 --> 00:14:08.040
Rimet, Rimet, Rimet.

00:14:08.460 --> 00:14:15.240
Er, plus 20% of the ship's course minus the pi-phigris theorem

00:14:15.240 --> 00:14:17.540
multiplied by two over the x-axis minus one

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:18.980
equals the total velocity of Red Dwarf,

00:14:19.020 --> 00:14:20.800
which means I know everything about astro-engineering.

00:14:20.900 --> 00:14:22.140
Good morning, Lister, probably the last time.

00:14:22.580 --> 00:14:25.990
You got it all down, have you, Rimet?

00:14:26.350 --> 00:14:27.850
Couple of blanks, but I think we're there.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:30.700
I can't remember anything.

00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:32.780
Think what you will, Lister.

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:35.210
F-I-S-H.

00:14:35.410 --> 00:14:36.430
That's how you spell fish.

00:14:36.630 --> 00:14:37.710
And you just keel over,

00:14:37.910 --> 00:14:39.750
I'm sure it'll all come flooding back to you.

00:14:40.630 --> 00:14:41.590
Try it, Lister.

00:14:44.580 --> 00:14:46.660
Will entrance for the engineer's examination

00:14:46.660 --> 00:14:48.660
now make their way to the teaching room?

00:14:49.560 --> 00:14:50.720
I'm not going to be honest with a good look.

00:14:53.340 --> 00:14:53.940
It's all right, Lister.

00:14:54.430 --> 00:14:56.510
I'm in complete and total control.

00:15:05.260 --> 00:15:07.270
Lock. Lock.

00:15:30.060 --> 00:15:32.400
Oh, you're getting really big now, you know.

00:15:33.220 --> 00:15:34.580
I hope it's not twins.

00:15:34.800 --> 00:15:36.040
You've already got all my milk ration.

00:15:36.750 --> 00:15:38.490
Never mind, when the baby cat comes,

00:15:38.710 --> 00:15:40.490
maybe we can give them water and pretend it's milk.

00:15:40.490 --> 00:15:42.090
It's only a baby cat, I won't know, eh?

00:15:42.630 --> 00:15:45.280
Eh, do you want to see me picture the Fiji again, Frankie?

00:15:45.730 --> 00:15:46.850
You're going to love it there.

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:47.520
Look.

00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:55.240
OK, everybody, you've got three hours.

00:15:55.600 --> 00:15:58.140
No modems, no speaking slide rules.

00:15:59.210 --> 00:15:59.970
Turn over and start.

00:16:00.090 --> 00:16:00.410
Good luck.

00:16:41.090 --> 00:16:47.510
Thank you.

00:17:14.900 --> 00:17:29.090
Where's the captain's office?

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:33.500
Over there, where it says Captain's Office, where it's always said Captain's Office.

00:17:33.500 --> 00:17:35.360
So that's the Captain's Office.

00:17:36.120 --> 00:17:36.920
So how are you, then?

00:17:37.310 --> 00:17:37.550
Right.

00:17:37.920 --> 00:17:39.040
Do you know what he wants to see me for?

00:17:39.580 --> 00:17:41.900
Yes, I think you've been promoted to Admiral.

00:17:42.470 --> 00:17:42.870
Oh, yeah?

00:17:43.260 --> 00:17:43.600
Yeah.

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:46.600
For your diligence and general devotion to duty.

00:17:47.240 --> 00:17:47.600
Oh, yeah?

00:17:48.380 --> 00:17:55.380
Lister, you asked to see me, Captain.

00:17:56.780 --> 00:17:57.460
Where's the cap?

00:17:58.800 --> 00:17:59.060
What?

00:18:00.280 --> 00:18:00.720
What cat?

00:18:01.360 --> 00:18:04.160
Lister, not only are you so stupid,

00:18:04.160 --> 00:18:06.380
you bring aboard an unquarantined animal

00:18:06.380 --> 00:18:08.820
and jeopardize every man and woman on this ship.

00:18:09.250 --> 00:18:13.220
Not only that, but you take a photograph of yourself with the cat

00:18:13.220 --> 00:18:15.580
and send it to be processed in the ship's lab.

00:18:17.020 --> 00:18:18.620
Now, I'm gonna ask you again.

00:18:18.800 --> 00:18:20.040
Do you have a cat?

00:18:20.340 --> 00:18:20.560
No.

00:18:21.260 --> 00:18:22.860
Have you got a cat?

00:18:23.460 --> 00:18:24.480
It's that one.

00:18:24.920 --> 00:18:26.020
Where'd you get it, Titan?

00:18:26.560 --> 00:18:26.640
Yes.

00:18:27.030 --> 00:18:29.570
Don't you realize that that thing could be carrying anything?

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:32.720
Don't you remember what happened on the Oregon with the rabbits?

00:18:33.240 --> 00:18:35.880
Lister, a loose animal aboard the ship could get anywhere.

00:18:36.140 --> 00:18:37.640
It could get into the air ducts.

00:18:37.700 --> 00:18:38.860
It could get into Holly.

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:42.080
You know, a little nibble here and a little nibble there, Lister,

00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:44.300
and before you know it, we're flying backwards.

00:18:44.810 --> 00:18:47.270
Now, I want that cat, and I want it now.

00:18:47.550 --> 00:18:50.530
Sir, just suppose I did have a cat.

00:18:50.670 --> 00:18:53.800
Just suppose, what would you do with Frankenstein?

00:18:54.350 --> 00:18:55.930
I'd send it down to the medical center,

00:18:55.950 --> 00:18:57.810
and I'd have it cut up and test run on it.

00:18:58.320 --> 00:18:59.880
Would you put it back together when you'd finished?

00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:02.980
Lister, the cat would be dead.

00:19:03.870 --> 00:19:05.710
So with respect, sir, what's in it for the cat?

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:08.040
Lister, give me that cat.

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:09.600
It's not as easy as that.

00:19:10.420 --> 00:19:12.360
Me and the cat, we're going to have a baby cat.

